import H0mework.NavierStokes.ShellSources.InfiniteLineageReceiptSquare

/-!
# Source completion of an infinite generated shell lineage

This module strengthens receipt-square decay to exact additive completion on
the whole flattened coefficient carrier.

For every actual lineage response, the old coefficient carrier and the new
receipt trace have disjoint supports.  Hence the next carrier's exact
coefficient mass is the old mass plus the source-generated receipt quantum.
Iteration gives

```text
mass(current n) = mass(seed) + ∑ i < n, q i.
```

The flattened carrier mass is then identified exactly with the finite-state
coefficient enstrophy used by the critical PDE consumer.  A common critical
margin therefore makes `∑ q i` summable, which is strictly stronger than the
previous square summability.

Finally, the difference between any two ordered prefix carriers is the
literal intervening receipt tail, and its exact coefficient mass is the
corresponding finite tail sum.  This is the finite-prefix Cauchy ledger for
the eventual whole `ℓ²` completion; no limit, convergence certificate,
support coverage, or silent-tail premise is stored in the source lineage.
-/

